     The "potion explodes" message occurs when a potion of acid  takes
water damage.  You've probably hit

   C343-179   fixed   If a monster is killed by a drawbridge while
carrying
   a potion of acid, the game may panic.

That description is overly specific, reflecting the bug report which
led
to its discovery:  "by a drawbridge" should be "over water".   When
some monster's inventory was dropped upon its death (or perhaps
the potion was picked up and then dropped by a live pet), a potion
of acid was destroyed.   But another part of the program was unaware
of that and went ahead and placed it on the map, accessing freed
memory in the process.  That could lead to a variety of symtoms,
including a segmentation fault or access violation, not just to the
panic mentioned in the bug entry.

     The dying monster was probably the victim of genocide.  Its
inventory couldn't be processed until you returned to reactivate the
level it was on.

